laborate with other students, and actively participate in rich virtual contexts (Gee 2003;Salen 2007;Shaffer 2006). Similarly, inquiry-based learning approaches for CS have yielded encouraging results that demonstrate improved student engagement (Hoffman et al. 2019), student achievement (Hoffman et al. 2019;Chen and Yang 2018), and student attitudes towards CS (Hoffman et al. 2019;Pollock et al. 2017). Inquiry-based learning approaches for CS are also being explored at the",
